.TH DANBY-FISHINGTWO 1
.SH NAME
danby-fishingtwo \- bioeconomics of two fish stocks and one fleet
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B danby/fishingtwo
.SH MODEL
Xi'=ri Xi(1-Xi/Ki)-qi E Xi;
E'=sE(p1q1X1+p2q2X2-c).
.PP
The same fishing effort E harvests both stocks.  Effort responds to combined
revenue per effort, so a valuable abundant species can maintain effort that
overexploits another species even when the latter alone would be unprofitable.
.SH DISPLAY
Two fish-stock histories and the fleet-effort history expose ecological and
economic coupling.  The shared client lays the ten controls out in two rows
so labels and direct manipulation remain legible.
.SH CONTROLS
Drag any state bar.  Tracks set growth, capacity, catchability, and price for
each stock, followed by fleet cost and response.  Space pauses, period steps,
r resets, and q exits.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/danby/plugin/fishingtwo.b
.br
.B /appl/danby/fishingtwo.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR danby-fishingone (1),
.IR populationmodel (2)
